      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 668391539,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The patch is fine in general. I would avoid casting to toStdStr and instead directly compare the QString with the char. It is a much safer option and will also take into consideration special characters (although the rpcap strings should only be ascii anyway).\n\nMy main issue is, that the remote capture dialog is still a TreeWidget, when local and pipes is already based on the InterfaceTreeModel. But this is a change for some other time. \n\nPlease fix the issues with the wording as well as the string comparison. The rest is fine by me.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
